
# Process: platform info and lifecycle. Platform implementation is selected at build time and hidden behind this API.

mark stable

load @term/base/native/{platform}/process
  find get-platform
  find exit-with

task platform
  like text
  send back
    call get-platform

task exit
  take code, like number
  like void
  call exit-with
    read code

# a spawned child process: the platform process object lives in the opaque `dock` handle, typed per backend.
# `id` is the worker number on the browser backend, where a Worker stands in for the process. A child that
# process/child `start` made is held by its runner under `handle`, a number, and keeps the `command` it runs and its
# `limit` in milliseconds (0 for none), which `wait` names when the limit ends it
form child
  link dock, mark private
  link
    id
    like size
    need false
  link
    handle
    like number
    fall 0
  link
    command
    like text
    fall text <>
  link
    limit
    like number
    fall 0
